2	title: "Phase 04: UI Overlays & Components"
3	description: "Replace all inline element.style.* assignments in utilities.js and ui.js with CSS class-based components. Add entrance animations. All card event popups, modals, toasts, and loading overlay use the design system from style.css."
4	skill: "none"
5	status: pending
6	group: "frontend-overhaul"
7	dependencies: ["phase-01-design-foundation", "phase-02-lobby-redesign", "phase-03-game-page-layout"]
8	tags: [phase, frontend, overlays, components, animation]
9	created: 2026-04-15
10	updated: 2026-04-15
11	---
12	
13	# Phase 04: UI Overlays & Components
14	
15	**Context:** [Master Plan](./plan.md) | **Dependencies:** P01–P03 | **Status:** Pending
16	
17	---
18	
19	## Overview
20	
21	The game's dynamic UI — card event popups, player selection modals, text input boxes, drinking prompts, toast notifications, and loading overlays — are all currently built by assigning inline `element.style.*` properties directly in JS. This phase replaces all of those with CSS class assignments, using the component classes defined in `style.css` (Phase 01). The result is consistent styling, smooth CSS animations, and maintainability.
22	
23	**Goal:** Every dynamically-created UI component (`createPopup`, `createPlayerSelector`, `createTextInput`, `createDrinkingPrompt`, `createReactionPrompt`, `showToast`, `showLoading`) uses only CSS classes — zero inline style assignments except for genuinely dynamic runtime values (timer countdown text, computed pixel positions).
24	
25	---
26	
27	## Context & Workflow
28	
29	### How This Phase Fits Into the Project
30	
31	- **Files changed:**
32	  - `game/static/utilities.js` — rewrite all five creator functions
33	  - `game/static/ui.js` — rewrite `showLoading`/`hideLoading`/`showToast`
34	  - `game/static/style.css` — add missing component variants needed by this phase
35	
36	- **No changes to:** `main.js`, `cards.js`, `app.js`, `webcam.js`
37	  - `cards.js` calls `createPopup(...)`, `createPlayerSelector(...)`, etc. with the same signatures — function signatures are preserved exactly
38	
39	### User Workflow
40	
41	**Trigger:** A player draws a card that has a special rule (e.g., "You" = card 2 = player selection).
42	
43	**Steps:**
44	1. Card drawn → `cards.js` calls `createPopup("Alex drew You!", 2000)` — styled popup appears center-screen with slide-up animation, auto-dismisses
45	2. If the current player: `createPlayerSelector(players, client, callback)` — modal with player buttons
46	3. Player selects a target → modal closes, game continues
47	
48	**Success Outcome:** All card events trigger visually polished overlays that match the site design — not raw inline-styled DOM elements.
49	
50	### Integration Points
51	
52	**Upstream Dependencies:**
53	- Phase 01: `.kc-overlay`, `.kc-popup`, `.kc-toast`, `.kc-spinner`, `.kc-loading-overlay`, `.kc-loading-box`, CSS custom properties, animations in `style.css`
54	- Phase 03: header is `z-index: 50` (Tailwind `z-50`). Overlays must use `var(--kc-z-modal)` = 1100 to appear above the header.
55	
56	---
57	
58	## Requirements
59	
60	### Functional
61	
62	- `createPopup(content, duration, buttons?)` — behavior unchanged (auto-dismiss after `duration`, optional buttons array)
63	- `createPlayerSelector(players, excludePlayer, callback)` — behavior unchanged
64	- `createTextInput(prompt, callback, timeout)` — behavior unchanged (countdown timer, Enter key submits)
65	- `createDrinkingPrompt(playerName, callback)` — behavior unchanged
66	- `createReactionPrompt(message, targetZone, callback)` — behavior unchanged
67	- `showToast(message, type, duration)` — behavior unchanged (types: `'info'`, `'error'`, `'success'`, `'warning'`)
68	- `showLoading(message)` / `hideLoading()` — behavior unchanged
69	
70	### Technical
71	
72	- Function signatures identical to current — `cards.js` and `main.js` call these without changes
73	- `export default` / `export` keywords unchanged
74	- No `element.style.*` property assignments except:
75	  - `element.style.opacity = '0'` for fade-out transitions on toast dismiss
76	  - Dynamic countdown text via `textContent`
77	  - Computed pixel positions if needed (none expected in this phase)
78	- All new DOM elements get `data-test` attributes matching their purpose for future test automation
79	- Overlays must render above the game header (z-index > 50 / `var(--kc-z-modal)`)
80	
81	---
82	
83	## Decision Log
84	
85	### Retain `element.style.opacity` for Toast Fade-out (ADR-04-01)
86	
87	**Date:** 2026-04-15
88	**Status:** Accepted
89	
90	**Context:** CSS `transition: opacity` requires setting `opacity: 0` via JS to trigger the fade-out before removal. This is a dynamic runtime value, not a static style.
