content.content:
1	---
2	title: "Phase 04: UI Overlays & Components"
3	description: "Replace all inline element.style.* assignments in utilities.js and ui.js with CSS class-based components. Add entrance animations. All card event popups, modals, toasts, and loading overlay use the design system from style.css."
4	skill: "none"
5	status: pending
6	group: "frontend-overhaul"
7	dependencies: ["phase-01-design-foundation", "phase-02-lobby-redesign", "phase-03-game-page-layout"]
8	tags: [phase, frontend, overlays, components, animation]
9	created: 2026-04-15
10	updated: 2026-04-15
11	---
12	
13	# Phase 04: UI Overlays & Components
14	
15	**Context:** [Master Plan](./plan.md) | **Dependencies:** P01–P03 | **Status:** Pending
16	
17	---
18	
19	## Overview
20	
21	The game's dynamic UI — card event popups, player selection modals, text input boxes, drinking prompts, toast notifications, and loading overlays — are all currently built by assigning inline `element.style.*` properties directly in JS. This phase replaces all of those with CSS class assignments, using the component classes defined in `style.css` (Phase 01). The result is consistent styling, smooth CSS animations, and maintainability.
22	
23	**Goal:** Every dynamically-created UI component (`createPopup`, `createPlayerSelector`, `createTextInput`, `createDrinkingPrompt`, `createReactionPrompt`, `showToast`, `showLoading`) uses only CSS classes — zero inline style assignments except for genuinely dynamic runtime values (timer countdown text, computed pixel positions).
24	
25	---
26	
27	## Context & Workflow
28	
29	### How This Phase Fits Into the Project
30	
31	- **Files changed:**
32	  - `game/static/utilities.js` — rewrite all five creator functions
33	  - `game/static/ui.js` — rewrite `showLoading`/`hideLoading`/`showToast`
34	  - `game/static/style.css` — add missing component variants needed by this phase
35	
36	- **No changes to:** `main.js`, `cards.js`, `app.js`, `webcam.js`
37	  - `cards.js` calls `createPopup(...)`, `createPlayerSelector(...)`, etc. with the same signatures — function signatures are preserved exactly
38	
39	### User Workflow
40	
41	**Trigger:** A player draws a card that has a special rule (e.g., "You" = card 2 = player selection).
42	
43	**Steps:**
44	1. Card drawn → `cards.js` calls `createPopup("Alex drew You!", 2000)` — styled popup appears center-screen with slide-up animation, auto-dismisses
45	2. If the current player: `createPlayerSelector(players, client, callback)` — modal with player buttons
46	3. Player selects a target → modal closes, game continues
47	
48	**Success Outcome:** All card events trigger visually polished overlays that match the site design — not raw inline-styled DOM elements.
49	
50	### Problem Being Solved
51	
52	**Pain Point:** Every card event currently creates DOM elements with dozens of `element.style.*` inline assignments scattered through `utilities.js` (e.g., `popup.style.background = 'rgba(0,0,0,0.9)'`, `playerBtn.style.fontSize = '16px'`). These inline styles cannot be overridden by CSS, are impossible to animate with CSS transitions, and create a maintenance nightmare where design changes require editing JS files. `ui.js` has a syntax error (`default export function`) that prevents it from loading at all in strict module environments.
53	
54	### Integration Points
55	
56	**Upstream Dependencies:**
57	- Phase 01: `.kc-overlay`, `.kc-popup`, `.kc-toast`, `.kc-spinner`, `.kc-loading-overlay`, `.kc-loading-box`, CSS custom properties, animations in `style.css`
58	- Phase 03: header is `z-index: 50` (Tailwind `z-50`). Overlays must use `var(--kc-z-modal)` = 1100 to appear above the header.
59	
60	---
61	
62	## Prerequisites & Clarifications
63	
64	### Prerequisites
65	
66	- [ ] Phase 01 complete — `.kc-overlay`, `.kc-overlay--modal`, `.kc-popup`, `.kc-toast`, `.kc-spinner`, `.kc-loading-overlay`, `.kc-loading-box`, `.kc-btn`, `.kc-input`, `@keyframes kc-slide-up` all defined in style.css
67	- [ ] Phase 03 complete — header at `z-50` (z-index 50) established; overlays at `var(--kc-z-modal)` = 1100 will render above it
68	- [ ] Dev server running (`npm run dev` in `game/`)
69	- [ ] `game/static/utilities.js` and `game/static/ui.js` are writable
70	
71	### Unresolved Questions
72	
73	None — function signatures are preserved per ADR-04-02; toast fade-out uses `style.opacity` per ADR-04-01.
74	
75	### Caution
76	
77	Test every card type after implementation — `cards.js` and `main.js` both call these functions dynamically (`import('./utilities.js').then(...)`). A function signature mismatch or export name change will silently break card events with no console error at load time (only at runtime when a card is drawn).
78	
79	---
80	
81	## Requirements
82	
83	### Functional
84	
85	- `createPopup(content, duration, buttons?)` — behavior unchanged (auto-dismiss after `duration`, optional buttons array)
86	- `createPlayerSelector(players, excludePlayer, callback)` — behavior unchanged
87	- `createTextInput(prompt, callback, timeout)` — behavior unchanged (countdown timer, Enter key submits)
88	- `createDrinkingPrompt(playerName, callback)` — behavior unchanged
89	- `createReactionPrompt(message, targetZone, callback)` — behavior unchanged
90	- `showToast(message, type, duration)` — behavior unchanged (types: `'info'`, `'error'`, `'success'`, `'warning'`)
91	- `showLoading(message)` / `hideLoading()` — behavior unchanged
92	
93	### Technical
94	
95	- Function signatures identical to current — `cards.js` and `main.js` call these without changes
96	- `export default` / `export` keywords unchanged
97	- No `element.style.*` property assignments except:
98	  - `element.style.opacity = '0'` for fade-out transitions on toast dismiss
99	  - Dynamic countdown text via `textContent`
100	  - Computed pixel positions if needed (none expected in this phase)
101	- All new DOM elements get `data-test` attributes matching their purpose for future test automation
102	- Overlays must render above the game header (z-index > 50 / `var(--kc-z-modal)`)
103	
104	---
105	
106	## Decision Log
107	
108	### Retain `element.style.opacity` for Toast Fade-out (ADR-04-01)
109	
110	**Date:** 2026-04-15
111	**Status:** Accepted
112	
113	**Context:** CSS `transition: opacity` requires setting `opacity: 0` via JS to trigger the fade-out before removal. This is a dynamic runtime value, not a static style.
114	
115	**Decision:** Allow `element.style.opacity = '0'` in the toast dismiss logic. All other styling uses classes.
116	
117	### Keep Existing Function Signatures (ADR-04-02)
118	
119	**Date:** 2026-04-15
120	**Status:** Accepted
121	
122	**Context:** `cards.js` calls all utility functions without imports (they're imported at the top of `utilities.js` and re-exported). Changing signatures would break 13 card event handlers.
123	
124	**Decision:** Keep function signatures identical. Only change the internal DOM construction implementation.
125	
126	---
127	
128	## Implementation Steps
129	
130	### Step 0: TDD
131	
132	This phase rewrites DOM-manipulation JS functions. There are no pure functions or data-transformation utilities to unit test.
133	
134	**Manual verification approach — run these after all steps complete:**
135	
136	1. Open two browser tabs, create a game, start it with 2 players
137	2. Draw a card that triggers each utility function:
138	   - Card that triggers `createPopup` (any card) → popup appears with slide-up animation, centered, above header
139	   - Card that triggers `createPlayerSelector` → modal with player buttons, styled, hover works
140	   - Card that triggers `createTextInput` → modal with input + countdown in red, Enter submits
141	   - Card that triggers `createDrinkingPrompt` → green "Done Drinking" button, closes on click
142	   - Trigger `showToast('Test', 'success')` in browser console → green toast appears and fades
143	   - Call `showLoading('Waiting…')` then `hideLoading()` in console → spinner overlay appears/disappears
144	3. Verify all overlays appear above the game header
145	4. Verify no `element.style.*` assignments remain in the new utilities.js or ui.js (except `toast.style.opacity = '0'`)
146	5. Check browser console — no JS errors throughout
147	
148	There is nothing to write before implementing. Proceed to Step 1.
149	
150	### Step 1: Add Additional Component Classes to `style.css`
151	
152	Append to `style.css`:
153	
154	```css
155	/* ----------------------------------------------------------
156	   Phase 04 Additions: Overlay component variants
157	   ---------------------------------------------------------- */
158	
159	/* Popup title highlight (card events use gold accent) */
160	.kc-popup-title-accent {
161	  color: var(--kc-accent);
162	  font-size: 1.35rem;
163	  font-weight: 700;
164	  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
165	}
166	
167	/* Player selector button */
168	.kc-player-select-btn {
169	  display: block;
170	  width: 100%;
171	  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
172	  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
173	  background: var(--kc-bg);
174	  border: 1px solid var(--kc-border);
175	  border-radius: var(--kc-radius-sm);
176	  font-size: 0.95rem;
177	  font-weight: 500;
178	  color: var(--kc-text);
179	  text-align: left;
180	  cursor: pointer;
181	  transition: background 0.12s, border-color 0.12s;
182	}
183	.kc-player-select-btn:hover {
184	  background: #eff6ff;
185	  border-color: var(--kc-accent);
186	  color: var(--kc-accent);
187	}
188	
189	/* Timer text in text-input rounds */
190	.kc-timer-text {
191	  font-size: 0.85rem;
192	  color: var(--kc-danger);
193	  font-weight: 600;
194	  margin-top: 0.75rem;
195	  text-align: center;
196	}
197	
198	/* Drinking prompt done button */
199	.kc-drinking-btn {
200	  margin-top: 1rem;
201	  width: 100%;
202	  padding: 0.75rem;
203	  background: var(--kc-success);
204	  color: #fff;
205	  border: none;
206	  border-radius: var(--kc-radius-sm);
207	  font-size: 1rem;
208	  font-weight: 600;
209	  cursor: pointer;
210	  transition: background 0.15s;
211	}
212	.kc-drinking-btn:hover {
213	  background: #16a34a;
214	}
215	
216	/* Reaction prompt action button */
217	.kc-reaction-btn {
218	  margin-top: 1rem;
219	  width: 100%;
220	  padding: 0.75rem;
221	  background: var(--kc-warning);
222	  color: var(--kc-text);
223	  border: none;
224	  border-radius: var(--kc-radius-sm);
225	  font-size: 1rem;
226	  font-weight: 600;
227	  cursor: pointer;
228	  transition: background 0.15s;
229	}
230	.kc-reaction-btn:hover {
231	  background: #d97706;
232	  color: #fff;
233	}
234	```
235	
236	### Step 2: Rewrite `utilities.js`
237	
238	Replace the entire file with:
239	
240	```js
241	// utilities.js
242	
243	// ── Math helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────
244	export function gaussianRandom(mean = 0, stdev = 1) {
245	    const u = 1 - Math.random();
246	    const v = Math.random();
247	    const z = Math.sqrt(-2.0 * Math.log(u)) * Math.cos(2.0 * Math.PI * v);
248	    return Math.round(z * stdev + mean);
249	}
250	
251	export function lerp(start, end, t) {
252	    return start * (1 - t) + end * t;
253	}
254	
255	export function easeInOutCubic(t) {
256	    return t < 0.5 ? 4 * t * t * t : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * t + 2, 3) / 2;
257	}
258	
259	// ── UI Helper: backdrop overlay ──────────────────────────────
260	// Uses .kc-overlay--modal modifier class for z-index tier (1100).
261	// Do NOT use style.zIndex — CSSOM silently discards var() references.
262	function createOverlay() {
263	    const overlay = document.createElement('div');
264	    overlay.className = 'kc-overlay kc-overlay--modal';
265	    return overlay;
266	}
267	
268	// ── createPopup ──────────────────────────────────────────────
269	// Shows a centered popup with optional action buttons.
270	// duration > 0: auto-dismisses after `duration` ms
271	// duration === 0: stays until manually closed
272	export function createPopup(content, duration = 3000, buttons = null) {
273	    const overlay = createOverlay();
274	
275	    const popup = document.createElement('div');
276	    popup.className = 'kc-popup';
277	    popup.setAttribute('data-test', 'card-event-popup');
278	    popup.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
279	    popup.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
280	
281	    const title = document.createElement('p');
282	    title.className = 'kc-popup-title-accent';
283	    title.textContent = content;
284	    popup.appendChild(title);
285	
286	    if (buttons && buttons.length > 0) {
287	        const btnRow = document.createElement('div');
288	        btnRow.className = 'flex gap-2 justify-end mt-4';
289	
290	        buttons.forEach(({ text, callback }) => {
291	            const btn = document.createElement('button');
292	            btn.className = 'kc-btn kc-btn-primary';
293	            btn.textContent = text;
294	            btn.onclick = () => {
295	                callback();
296	                if (document.body.contains(overlay)) document.body.removeChild(overlay);
297	            };
298	            btnRow.appendChild(btn);
299	        });
300	
301	        popup.appendChild(btnRow);
302	    }
303	
304	    overlay.appendChild(popup);
305	    document.body.appendChild(overlay);
306	
307	    if (duration > 0) {
308	        setTimeout(() => {
309	            if (document.body.contains(overlay)) document.body.removeChild(overlay);
310	        }, duration);
311	    }
312	
313	    return overlay;
314	}
315	
316	// ── createPlayerSelector ─────────────────────────────────────
317	// Shows a modal with a button per selectable player.
318	export function createPlayerSelector(players, excludePlayer, callback) {
319	    const overlay = createOverlay();
320	
321	    const panel = document.createElement('div');
322	    panel.className = 'kc-popup';
323	    panel.setAttribute('data-test', 'player-selector');
324	    panel.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
325	    panel.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
326	
327	    const heading = document.createElement('h3');
328	    heading.textContent = 'Choose a Player';
329	    panel.appendChild(heading);
330	
331	    const list = document.createElement('div');
332	    list.className = 'mt-3 flex flex-col gap-1';
333	
334	    const available = players.filter(p => p !== excludePlayer);
335	    available.forEach(player => {
336	        const btn = document.createElement('button');
337	        btn.className = 'kc-player-select-btn';
338	        btn.textContent = player;
339	        btn.setAttribute('data-test', `select-player-${player}`);
340	        btn.onclick = () => {
341	            callback(player);
342	            if (document.body.contains(overlay)) document.body.removeChild(overlay);
343	        };
344	        list.appendChild(btn);
345	    });
346	
347	    panel.appendChild(list);
348	    overlay.appendChild(panel);
349	    document.body.appendChild(overlay);
350	
351	    return overlay;
352	}
353	
354	// ── createTextInput ───────────────────────────────────────────
355	// Shows a modal with a text input and countdown timer.
356	export function createTextInput(prompt, callback, timeout = 30000) {
357	    const overlay = createOverlay();
358	
359	    const panel = document.createElement('div');
360	    panel.className = 'kc-popup';
361	    panel.setAttribute('data-test', 'text-input-panel');
362	    panel.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
363	    panel.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
364	
365	    const heading = document.createElement('h3');
366	    heading.textContent = prompt;
367	    panel.appendChild(heading);
368	
369	    const input = document.createElement('input');
370	    input.type = 'text';
371	    input.className = 'kc-input mt-3';
372	    input.setAttribute('data-test', 'text-input-field');
373	    input.placeholder = 'Type here…';
374	    panel.appendChild(input);
375	
376	    const submitBtn = document.createElement('button');
377	    submitBtn.className = 'kc-btn kc-btn-primary w-full mt-3';
378	    submitBtn.textContent = 'Submit';
379	    submitBtn.setAttribute('data-test', 'text-input-submit');
380	    panel.appendChild(submitBtn);
381	
382	    const timerEl = document.createElement('p');
383	    timerEl.className = 'kc-timer-text';
384	    panel.appendChild(timerEl);
385	
386	    let timeLeft = Math.floor(timeout / 1000);
387	    timerEl.textContent = `${timeLeft}s remaining`;
388	
389	    const timer = setInterval(() => {
390	        timeLeft--;
391	        timerEl.textContent = `${timeLeft}s remaining`;
392	        if (timeLeft <= 0) {
393	            clearInterval(timer);
394	            callback('');
395	            if (document.body.contains(overlay)) document.body.removeChild(overlay);
396	        }
397	    }, 1000);
398	
399	    const handleSubmit = () => {
400	        clearInterval(timer);
401	        callback(input.value);
402	        if (document.body.contains(overlay)) document.body.removeChild(overlay);
403	    };
404	
405	    submitBtn.onclick = handleSubmit;
406	    input.addEventListener('keypress', e => {
407	        if (e.key === 'Enter') handleSubmit();
408	    });
409	
410	    overlay.appendChild(panel);
411	    document.body.appendChild(overlay);
412	
413	    input.focus();
414	    return overlay;
415	}
416	
417	// ── createDrinkingPrompt ──────────────────────────────────────
418	// Shows a modal prompting the named player to confirm drinking.
419	export function createDrinkingPrompt(playerName, callback) {
420	    const overlay = createOverlay();
421	
422	    const panel = document.createElement('div');
423	    panel.className = 'kc-popup text-center';
424	    panel.setAttribute('data-test', 'drinking-prompt');
425	    panel.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
426	    panel.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
427	
428	    const msg = document.createElement('p');
429	    msg.className = 'kc-popup-title-accent';
430	    msg.textContent = `${playerName}, click when you're done drinking!`;
431	    panel.appendChild(msg);
432	
433	    const btn = document.createElement('button');
434	    btn.className = 'kc-drinking-btn';
435	    btn.textContent = 'Done Drinking';
436	    btn.setAttribute('data-test', 'drinking-done-btn');
437	    btn.onclick = () => {
438	        callback();
439	        if (document.body.contains(overlay)) document.body.removeChild(overlay);
440	    };
441	    panel.appendChild(btn);
442	
443	    overlay.appendChild(panel);
444	    document.body.appendChild(overlay);
445	
446	    return overlay;
447	}
448	
449	// ── createReactionPrompt ──────────────────────────────────────
450	// Shows a popup instructing the player to move mouse to a zone.
451	// Monitors mousemove on the canvas to detect if player reacted.
452	export function createReactionPrompt(message, targetZone, callback) {
453	    const overlay = createPopup(message, 0);
454	
455	    let reacted = false;
456	    const startTime = Date.now();
457	
458	    const checkReaction = (event) => {
459	        if (reacted) return;
460	
461	        const canvas = document.querySelector('#gameCanvas');
462	        if (!canvas) return;
463	
464	        const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
465	        const x = event.clientX - rect.left;
466	        const y = event.clientY - rect.top;
467	
468	        let inZone = false;
469	        if (targetZone === 'top')    inZone = y < rect.height * 0.2;
470	        if (targetZone === 'bottom') inZone = y > rect.height * 0.8;
471	
472	        if (inZone) {
473	            reacted = true;
474	            const reactionTime = Date.now() - startTime;
475	            callback(reactionTime);
476	            if (document.body.contains(overlay)) document.body.removeChild(overlay);
477	            document.removeEventListener('mousemove', checkReaction);
478	        }
479	    };
480	
481	    document.addEventListener('mousemove', checkReaction);
482	    return overlay;
483	}
484	```
485	
486	### Step 3: Rewrite `ui.js`
487	
488	Replace the entire file with:
489	
490	```js
491	// ui.js — UI helper functions for Kings Cup
492	
493	// Show a loading spinner overlay
494	export default function showLoading(message = 'Loading…') {
495	    let overlay = document.getElementById('kc-loading-overlay');
496	    if (!overlay) {
497	        overlay = document.createElement('div');
498	        overlay.id = 'kc-loading-overlay';
499	        overlay.className = 'kc-loading-overlay';
500	        overlay.setAttribute('role', 'status');
501	        overlay.setAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');
502	
503	        const box = document.createElement('div');
504	        box.className = 'kc-loading-box';
505	
506	        const spinner = document.createElement('span');
507	        spinner.className = 'kc-spinner';
508	        spinner.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
509	
510	        const text = document.createElement('span');
511	        text.id = 'kc-loading-text';
512	        text.textContent = message;
513	
514	        box.appendChild(spinner);
515	        box.appendChild(text);
516	        overlay.appendChild(box);
517	        document.body.appendChild(overlay);
518	    } else {
519	        const text = document.getElementById('kc-loading-text');
520	        if (text) text.textContent = message;
521	        overlay.classList.remove('kc-hidden');
522	    }
523	}
524	
525	// Hide the loading spinner overlay
526	export function hideLoading() {
527	    const overlay = document.getElementById('kc-loading-overlay');
528	    if (overlay) overlay.classList.add('kc-hidden');
529	}
530	
531	// Show a toast notification
532	// type: 'info' | 'success' | 'error' | 'warning'
533	export function showToast(message, type = 'info', duration = 2500) {
534	    const toast = document.createElement('div');
535	    toast.className = `kc-toast kc-toast-${type}`;
536	    toast.setAttribute('role', 'alert');
537	    toast.setAttribute('data-test', 'toast');
538	    toast.textContent = message;
539	
540	    document.body.appendChild(toast);
541	
542	    setTimeout(() => {
543	        toast.style.opacity = '0';
544	        setTimeout(() => {
545	            if (document.body.contains(toast)) document.body.removeChild(toast);
546	        }, 350);
547	    }, duration);
548	}
549	
550	// Focus trap for modals — call after appending modal to DOM
551	export function trapFocus(modal) {
552	    const focusable = modal.querySelectorAll(
553	        'button, [href], input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])'
554	    );
555	    if (!focusable.length) return;
556	    const first = focusable[0];
557	    const last = focusable[focusable.length - 1];
558	
559	    modal.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
560	        if (e.key !== 'Tab') return;
561	        if (e.shiftKey) {
562	            if (document.activeElement === first) { last.focus(); e.preventDefault(); }
563	        } else {
564	            if (document.activeElement === last) { first.focus(); e.preventDefault(); }
565	        }
566	    });
567	
568	    first.focus();
569	}
570	```
571	
572	**Note:** `showLoading` is the `export default`. Currently, `main.js` does **not** import `ui.js` — `showLoading`, `hideLoading`, and `showToast` are not wired to `main.js`. If these functions need to be called from `main.js` in the future, add:
573	```js
574	import showLoading, { hideLoading, showToast, trapFocus } from './ui.js';
575	```
576	No import change is required for this phase — the rewrite is a drop-in replacement with the syntax error fixed.
577	
578	### Step 4: Verify `ui.js` syntax (export default)
579	
580	The current `ui.js` has a syntax error on line 4:
581	```js
582	default export function showLoading(...)
583	```
584	It should be:
585	```js
586	export default function showLoading(...)
587	```
588	The rewrite in Step 3 corrects this.
